function getTimeGreeting(){const h=new Date().getHours();if(h>=5&&h<12)return{greeting:"Good morning. 🌸",sub:"What's on your heart before the day takes over?"};if(h>=12&&h<17)return{greeting:"Hey, sis. 🌿",sub:"How are you actually doing right now?"};if(h>=17&&h<20)return{greeting:"You made it through. 🍂",sub:"The day is winding down. How are you feeling?"};return{greeting:"Still up? 🌙",sub:"Sometimes the quietest hours hold the most honest thoughts."};}
const HALLIE_DESK_NOTES=["Real talk — we apologize for taking up space even in our own journals. You don't have to do that here. Write messy. Write honest. Write the version nobody else gets to see. 🌿","Healing isn't linear. Neither is growth. Some weeks you'll write every day. Some weeks life gets loud and you won't. Both count. You're still in it either way. 💛","The entries that feel too small to write — 'I was tired today. I made tea. I just existed.' — those are the ones you'll treasure most someday. Don't edit your life. Just write it. 🌿","I built this because I needed it. A space that felt soft. That didn't rush me. That felt like a friend sitting across from me who actually gets it. I hope it feels that way for you too. 💌","This week, try writing without a prompt. Just open a new entry and let whatever comes, come. The first sentence is always the hardest. After that, you'll surprise yourself. ✨","You are not behind. Not in your healing, not in your life, not in any of it. You're exactly where you're supposed to be. Now write about it. 🌸","The feelings we keep avoiding are usually the ones that need the most room. What have you been dancing around lately? Today might be the day you finally say it. 🌿"];
